---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
---
<Base title="Trend Line" current="trend"
  description="How much of the IDX listing is testing its own 200-week moving average, and how much has broken below it.">

  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <div class="kicker">Trend Line · <span id="universe-count">—</span> stocks with a 200-week line</div>
      <h1>Who's testing their 200-week average</h1>
      <p class="dek">A stock's 200-week average — its price over roughly the last 3.8 years — is a slow line long-term
        holders watch as support. This page counts how many stocks sit right at their own line, and how many have
        broken below it.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="hero" aria-label="Latest reading">
      <div class="hero-lead">
        <div class="hero-label">Within 5% of their line · <span id="hero-date">latest session</span></div>
        <div class="hero-figure" id="near-pct">—</div>
        <div class="hero-verdict" id="near-verdict">Reading the record…</div>
        <dl class="hero-meta">
          <div><dt>A year ago</dt><dd id="near-year">—</dd></div>
          <div><dt>On record</dt><dd><span id="near-pctile">—</span> pctile</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="tiles">
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Near the line</div><div class="tile-value" id="n-near">—</div><svg class="tile-spark" id="near-spark" aria-hidden="true"></svg><div class="tile-note">Within ±5%, either side</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Below the line</div><div class="tile-value down" id="n-below">—</div><svg class="tile-spark" id="below-spark" aria-hidden="true"></svg><div class="tile-note"><span id="pct-below">—</span> of the universe</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Above the line</div><div class="tile-value up" id="n-above">—</div><div class="tile-note"><span id="pct-above">—</span> of the universe</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Broken deep</div><div class="tile-value down" id="n-deep">—</div><div class="tile-note">More than 30% below</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Median distance</div><div class="tile-value" id="median-dist">—</div><div class="tile-note">Middle stock vs its line</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Far above</div><div class="tile-value up" id="n-far">—</div><div class="tile-note">More than 50% above</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="figure-grid">
      <Figure no="Fig. I" title="Testing the line" chart="near" size="short"
        dek="Share of stocks within 5% of their own 200-week average, day by day." />
      <Figure no="Fig. II" title="Below the line" chart="below" size="short"
        dek="Share trading under their own 200-week average. Above 50%, most of the market is." />
    </div>

    <Figure no="Fig. III" title="Where every stock sits"
      dek="Each bar counts the stocks in a 5% band of distance from their own line. Gold is the ±5% band this page calls near.">
      <div class="spread-readout" style="display:flex; gap:14px; align-items:baseline; min-height:2.4em; padding-bottom:10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule-soft)">
        <span class="kicker" id="hist-label" style="color:var(--ink-faint)">Distribution</span>
        <span id="hist-readout" style="font: 400 1.15rem/1.3 var(--display)">Hover a bar to read it.</span>
      </div>
      <svg id="hist" viewBox="0 0 1000 220" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-labelledby="hist-alt" style="display:block;width:100%;height:220px;margin-top:12px;touch-action:pan-y"></svg>
      <p id="hist-alt" class="visually-hidden"></p>
      <div id="hist-axis" style="position:relative;height:1.6rem;font:500 .7rem/1 var(--mono);color:var(--ink-soft)" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <Fragment slot="how">
        <p>Distance is the latest close against the stock's own 200-week average: −20% means 20% below its line.
          Everything beyond +150% is folded into the last bar. Sitting near a 200-week average has no fixed meaning by
          itself — it can be a level that holds, or one that gets cut straight through.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>
  </div>

  <div class="toolbar">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="toolbar-label" id="band-label">Show</span>
      <div class="segmented" id="band" role="group" aria-labelledby="band-label">
        <button type="button" data-band="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
        <button type="button" data-band="near" aria-pressed="false">Near ±5%</button>
        <button type="button" data-band="below" aria-pressed="false">Below</button>
        <button type="button" data-band="above" aria-pressed="false">Above</button>
      </div>
      <span class="spacer"></span>
      <input type="search" id="search-input" class="search" placeholder="Ticker…" aria-label="Filter by ticker">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="figure" aria-label="Tables">
      <div class="tabs-head">
        <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a table">
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-a" aria-pressed="true" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-a">Closest to their line</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-b" aria-pressed="false" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-b">The daily record</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="panel-a" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-a">
        <div class="table-tools">
          <p class="figure-dek" style="margin:0">Every stock with a 200-week average, nearest its line first, whichever side.</p>
          <span class="table-count" id="row-count"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table id="data-table" class="data-table"></table></div>
        <div class="table-more"><button type="button" class="btn" id="row-more" hidden>Show all</button></div>
      </div>
      <div id="panel-b" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-b" hidden>
        <div class="table-tools">
          <input type="search" id="trend-date-filter" class="search" placeholder="Find a day — 2026-03…" aria-label="Filter the daily record by date">
          <span class="table-count" id="trend-count"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table id="trend-table" class="data-table"></table></div>
        <div class="table-more"><button type="button" class="btn" id="trend-more" hidden>Show all</button></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="figure" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="figure-head">
        <span class="figure-no">Method</span>
        <h2 id="method-title">Terms of the reading</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="method">
        <div><dt>The line</dt><dd>A simple average of the last <b>200 weekly closes</b>, on the dividend- and
          split-adjusted price, so an ex-dividend day never reads as a fake drop toward the line. A week's close is
          the latest price in it, including a week still in progress.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Near</dt><dd>Within <b>5%</b> either side of the line. Close from above and from below both count —
          the reading is about proximity, not which side.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>A stock needs about <b>3.8 years</b> of history to have a line at all, so recent
          listings are left out rather than estimated.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Not a signal</dt><dd>This page counts proximity; it does not predict which way a stock breaks.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script src="../lib/trend.js"></script>
</Base>
